WEBVTT

00:00:00.121 --> 00:00:02.811
Hello, and a very warm welcome to Shah Spectrum.

00:00:02.811 --> 00:00:05.979
If you're new here, welcome.

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:11.160
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us once more.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.965
Two of the best-known companies in the world, one man at the top of both, and a

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:16.565
question:

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.148
should they become one?

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:20.264
Hi, I'm Mittal Shah.

00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:26.120
This is an AI-generated version of my voice, and it is narrating today's story.

00:00:27.066 --> 00:00:28.464
Let's start with what happened.

00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:33.497
On the twentieth of October, on SpaceX's earnings call, Elon Musk said that Tesla

00:00:33.497 --> 00:00:38.856
and SpaceX have each set up a special committee to look at a possible merger.

00:00:38.856 --> 00:00:44.052
A special committee is a group of independent directors, board members with no

00:00:44.052 --> 00:00:49.248
personal stake, who study a deal on behalf of ordinary shareholders.

00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:55.883
Musk said he is a conflicted party, because he is a leader and a big owner of both

00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:59.309
companies, so he cannot take part in those discussions.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:02.016
He said he thinks a merger would be a good idea.

00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:06.482
But he also said that calling a deal certain would be overstating it.

00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:11.995
No price, no structure and no timetable has been announced.

00:01:12.676 --> 00:01:14.801
Now, who are the two companies?

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:20.189
Tesla makes electric cars, and is pushing into self-driving taxis and humanoid

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:20.789
robots.

00:01:20.652 --> 00:01:21.808
SpaceX builds rockets.

00:01:21.808 --> 00:01:24.950
It listed on the Nasdaq stock exchange in June this year.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:31.441
And in February it took over x-A-I, Musk's artificial intelligence company, which

00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:32.905
makes the Grok chatbot.

00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:37.925
This would not be the first time Musk's businesses have combined.

00:01:37.925 --> 00:01:42.463
In March last year, x-A-I took over X, the social media platform.

00:01:42.463 --> 00:01:44.751
This February, SpaceX took over x-A-I.

00:01:44.751 --> 00:01:48.886
So a Tesla and SpaceX merger would be the next step in a pattern, not a bolt from

00:01:48.886 --> 00:01:50.122
the blue.

00:01:51.131 --> 00:01:51.964
So why would they join?

00:01:51.964 --> 00:01:54.130
Musk's reason is artificial intelligence.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:02:01.363
He said there is a lot to be gained from working together on A-I software, chips,

00:02:01.363 --> 00:02:03.334
robotics and connectivity.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:09.096
They already cooperate on a chip factory called Terafab, and Tesla already holds

00:02:09.096 --> 00:02:12.382
SpaceX shares through an earlier investment in x-A-I.

00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:14.983
Here is why this is not simple:

00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:15.583
control.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.464
Musk owns about a fifth of Tesla.

00:02:17.464 --> 00:02:23.615
At SpaceX, press reports of the company's filings say he holds more than eighty per

00:02:23.615 --> 00:02:25.587
cent of the votes, through a special class of shares.

00:02:25.587 --> 00:02:28.933
Two companies, two very different ownership set-ups.

00:02:28.933 --> 00:02:32.885
A merger would have to settle how that is handled.

00:02:33.369 --> 00:02:35.345
Then there is the vote.

00:02:35.345 --> 00:02:40.365
Musk said a deal would need the approval of more than half of all Tesla shares, not

00:02:40.365 --> 00:02:42.391
just the shares that are voted.

00:02:42.391 --> 00:02:44.642
He called that quite a high hurdle.

00:02:44.642 --> 00:02:49.654
In practice, a share that is never voted counts the same as a vote against.

00:02:50.208 --> 00:02:51.133
A quick recap:

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:57.523
the committees exist, Musk is stepping aside, and Tesla's shareholders would face a

00:02:57.523 --> 00:02:58.123
high bar.

00:02:58.436 --> 00:02:59.234
What comes next?

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:02.804
Tesla's yearly shareholder meeting is on the third of December.

00:03:02.804 --> 00:03:07.127
Its published agenda has no merger vote on it.

00:03:07.127 --> 00:03:12.877
One report, citing unnamed sources, says the aim is to announce a deal in the first

00:03:12.877 --> 00:03:14.192
half of next year.

00:03:14.192 --> 00:03:16.002
That is a report, not a confirmed plan.

00:03:16.002 --> 00:03:22.591
Regulators and politics could also play a part, since both companies do business

00:03:22.591 --> 00:03:23.292
with governments.

00:03:23.743 --> 00:03:24.618
What do we not know?

00:03:24.618 --> 00:03:28.523
We do not know whether the committees will recommend a deal at all.

00:03:28.523 --> 00:03:34.092
We do not know what it would look like, or what shareholders would be offered.

00:03:34.092 --> 00:03:36.707
Talks like these can end with no deal.

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:38.061
To sum up:

00:03:38.061 --> 00:03:43.073
Tesla and SpaceX are studying a merger, Musk is staying out of the talks, and there

00:03:43.073 --> 00:03:46.022
is no deal, no terms and a high shareholder bar.

00:03:46.622 --> 00:03:50.358
This is news and explanation, not investment advice.

00:03:51.335 --> 00:03:54.564
Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode.

